&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;As part of Waymo&#39;s Legal team, you will work on the exciting legal issues surrounding our transformational autonomous driving technology and help drive our business lines forward from technology ideation through scaled commercial deployment. We partner with our public policy, safety, security and privacy experts to define transportation policy for the autonomous driving world to come, advising on regulatory changes that support and protect our users around the world. We collaborate with our engineering, product, strategy and operations teams to develop and protect our intellectual property portfolio and drive our corporate and commercial transactions. We ensure compliance with an increasingly complex and dynamic range of global regulations. And we anticipate, mitigate, and litigate high-profile and precedent-setting legal matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In this hybrid role, you will report into our Managing Counsel.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary, on-the-ground Privacy Counsel for Waymo&#39;s operations, product launches, and engineering initiatives across Germany and the broader EU, acting as a trusted advisor to ensure compliance with GDPR, ePrivacy, and local laws like the BDSG.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise on &quot;Privacy by Design&quot; and data minimization principles for European market entry, working directly with Product, Engineering, and AI/ML teams to design innovative privacy solutions for complex sensor data and model training. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively build and maintain constructive relationships with EU Data Protection Authorities (DPAs), acting as the primary legal contact for regulatory inquiries, data protection impact assessments (DPIAs), audits, and ongoing local engagement. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead rapid, localized legal response for any EU data incidents, coordinating internal investigations and compliance reviews, managing strict notification timelines, and mitigating regulatory risk. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Waymo’s Public Policy, Trust &amp;amp; Safety, and Regulatory Affairs teams to monitor, review, and help shape emerging European privacy legislation, developing advocacy strategies to influence policy changes that support responsible innovation. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Juris Doctor (or equivalent law degree) and active qualification to practice law in Germany (e.g., Volljurist) or another relevant EU jurisdiction. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of legal experience with significant expertise in European privacy, data protection, and regulatory compliance, preferably in-house at a global technology company. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep, practical expertise in the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and German national data protection laws (BDSG), with a track record of operationalizing these frameworks for complex data flows. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience engaging with European Data Protection Authorities (DPAs) and working with government or regulatory bodies to navigate rulemaking processes and compliance readiness. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising on cross-border data transfers, international data governance, and translating strict legal requirements into practical engineering specifications. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional fluency in both German and English, with exceptional ability to communicate legal risks clearly to leadership and technical teams in the face of ambiguity. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recognized European privacy certifications, such as CIPP/E, CIPM, or CIPT. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior in-house experience at a US-based multinational technology company, autonomous vehicle developer, or AI-focused enterprise navigating EU expansion. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience advising on the intersection of GDPR with emerging European technology and data regulations (e.g., the AI Act, Data Act), including experience providing counsel on proposed legislation. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience structuring and defending main establishment strategies (One-Stop-Shop) and data transfer frameworks for EU resident data. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in responding to privacy litigation, localized incident response, or managing comprehensive privacy compliance audits. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A technical background or strong fluency in data infrastructure, cloud computing, computer vision, or software engineering. &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Teneo is seeking a high-calibre Director to join our team in Berlin. This is a senior, client-facing role for an experienced Public Affairs Director advisor. The successful candidate will bring a strong network across German blue-chip companies and listed businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Managing Director in Teneo Strategy &amp;amp; Communications business in Europe, you will be responsible for building trusted senior client relationships, developing new revenue opportunities, leading complex client mandates and contributing to the growth and reputation of the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Based in Munich or Frankfurt, you will work closely with Teneo colleagues across Europe and the global network to deliver integrated advice to clients. This will include collaboration with specialists in corporate reputation, crisis preparedness and response, public affairs, geopolitics, management consulting, risk advisory, people advisory, sustainability, digital and creative campaigning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires both strategic advisory excellence and a strong commercial mindset. The successful candidate will be expected to bring market credibility, senior relationships, origination capability and the ability to lead multidisciplinary teams through complex, high-profile and often sensitive client situations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business Development and Market Growth&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the growth of Teneo Europe’s Corporate and Crisis Communications business from Germany by originating, winning and leading high-value client engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage an established network of senior relationships across German corporates and major organisations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and convert new business opportunities across corporate communications, corporate reputation, issues management, crisis preparedness and response, and special situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help position Teneo as a premier corporate and crisis communications adviser in Germany and the wider European region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Client Counsel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as trusted adviser to CEOs, supervisory and management boards, senior executives and communications and corporate affairs directors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide senior strategic counsel on corporate narrative, reputation, stakeholder engagement, issues management and crisis preparedness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise clients on how to communicate effectively with employees, media, government, regulators, customers, investors, partners and other key stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring judgement, discretion and confidence to high-pressure situations involving complex stakeholder dynamics, significant public scrutiny and reputational risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Corporate Communications and Crisis Situations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead communications strategies around major corporate events, business transformation, leadership change, restructuring, litigation, regulatory scrutiny, operational incidents, cyber incidents, activism and other significant or sensitive situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise clients on crisis preparedness, scenario planning, crisis governance, response strategies, messaging and stakeholder engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with legal advisers, public affairs teams, risk specialists, management consultants and other advisers to ensure communications strategies are aligned with broader business objectives and stakeholder considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide senior leadership in fast-moving and high-pressure situations involving intense scrutiny, competing stakeholder expectations and significant reputational risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Media, Reputation and Stakeholder Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute media strategies involving German, European and international business, corporate and national media.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise clients on reputation management, corporate positioning, proactive storytelling, executive positioning, crisis situations and complex issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help organisations build and protect trust with their most important stakeholders through clear, credible and consistent communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide senior counsel on emerging reputational risks, stakeholder expectations and issues that may affect corporate licence to operate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will bring:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong track record in corporate communications, corporate reputation, crisis communications, issues management, strategic communications, corporate affairs or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant senior-level experience, likely 15+ years, gained in an advisory firm, major corporation, consultancy, corporate affairs function, communications agency or other relevant environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven record of originating and winning major client mandates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the German corporate landscape, media environment, stakeholder expectations, reputational dynamics and the issues facing major businesses and their leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience advising CEOs, boards, senior executives and communications and corporate affairs leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable experience in one or more of the following: corporate reputation, crisis preparedness and response, issues management, business transformation, leadership transitions, litigation and regulatory communications, activism, restructuring, cyber incidents or other special situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An established senior network across German corporates, business leaders, communications and corporate affairs professionals, advisers, policymakers and media.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial judgement, including experience managing revenue, profitability, forecasting and client growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to lead complex, multidisciplinary teams and deliver high-quality work in demanding and high-pressure situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant senior-level experience, likely, 15+ years, gained in an advisory firm, listed company, financial institution, investor relations function, consultancy or other relevant environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven record of originating and winning major client mandates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Teneo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Teneo is the global CEO advisory firm. We partner with our clients globally to do great things for a better future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drawing upon our global team and expansive network of senior advisors, we provide advisory services across our five business segments on a stand-alone or fully integrated basis to help our clients solve complex business challenges. Our clients include a significant number of the Fortune 100 and FTSE 100, as well as other corporations, financial institutions, and organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our full range of advisory services includes strategic communications, investor relations, financial transactions and restructuring, management consulting, physical and cyber risk, organizational design, board and executive search, geopolitics and government affairs, corporate governance, ESG and DE&amp;amp;I.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The firm has more than 2,000 employees located in 50+ offices around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h3&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Teneo is seeking a high-calibre Director to join our team in Frankfurt. This is a senior, client-facing role for an experienced FinComms Director. As a Director, you’ll be responsible for providing the highest quality of service to our clients, playing a pivotal role in leading multiple, high-profile account teams, giving strategic counsel to senior clients, regularly providing insight and analysis across our business, and proactively contributing to developing additional business opportunities with existing clients and prospects. Directors manage and coach Senior Consultants and Consultants, and work into and learn from Managing Directors and Senior Managing Directors.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Role Overview&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Director in Teneo Strategy &amp;amp; Communications business in Europe, you will be responsible for building trusted senior client relationships, leading complex client mandates, team leadership, and contributing to the growth and reputation of the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Based in Frankfurt, you will work closely with Teneo colleagues across Europe and the global network to deliver integrated advice to clients. This will include collaboration with specialists in corporate reputation, crisis preparedness and response, public affairs, geopolitics, management consulting, risk advisory, people advisory, sustainability, digital and creative campaigning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Director at Teneo, you will be:&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading large and often integrated teams to develop and deliver financial communications that have real impact for our clients&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing team direction and management whilst acting as the day to day point of contact for clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for client servicing, profitability, forecasting and budgeting&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generating new business leads through networks and proactive opportunity spotting&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing insight and intelligence to the business through your experience and network&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively contributing to and fostering the development of junior team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenging the status quo with new thinking, new product development, and new ways of working&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and Experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years’ experience of working in a senior role in financial communications / IR advisory or in-house&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable experience in managing teams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Financially literate with excellent working knowledge of financial reporting and corporate transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent understanding of financial markets and business media&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent ability to shape and deliver strategic advice to senior level clients&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to manage and mentor junior staff&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An engaging self-starter with high attention to detail&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptionally strong verbal and written communication skills&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborator who is able to foster good working relationships&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time management and the ability to prioritise a varied workload&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable taking the lead on driving performance and revenue&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Teneo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Teneo is the global CEO advisory firm. We partner with our clients globally to do great things for a better future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drawing upon our global team and expansive network of senior advisors, we provide advisory services across our five business segments on a stand-alone or fully integrated basis to help our clients solve complex business challenges. Our clients include a significant number of the Fortune 100 and FTSE 100, as well as other corporations, financial institutions, and organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our full range of advisory services includes strategic communications, investor relations, financial transactions and restructuring, management consulting, physical and cyber risk, organizational design, board and executive search, geopolitics and government affairs, corporate governance, ESG and DE&amp;amp;I.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The firm has more than 2,000 employees located in 50+ offices around the world.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;𝗪𝗵𝗮𝘁 𝗠𝗮𝗸𝗲𝘀 𝗖𝗹𝗼𝘂𝗱𝗯𝗲𝗱𝘀 𝗨𝗻𝗶𝗾𝘂𝗲&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cloudbeds.com/&quot;&gt;Cloudbeds&lt;/a&gt;, we&#39;re not just building software, we&#39;re transforming hospitality. Our platform powers hotels across 150 countries, processing billions in bookings annually. From boutique properties to large hotel groups, we help hoteliers transform operations and uplevel their commercial strategy through a unified platform that integrates with hundreds of partners. And we do it with a completely remote team. Imagine working alongside global innovators to build AI-powered solutions that solve hoteliers&#39; biggest challenges. Since our founding in 2012, we&#39;ve continually been recognized for excellence, most recently earning top honors at the 2026 HotelTechAwards for Best Hotel Management Software and landing on Deloitte&#39;s Technology Fast 500 again, but we&#39;re just getting started.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How You&#39;ll Make an Impact:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Global Director, Mid-Market Onboarding, you will own and scale the onboarding function for Cloudbeds&#39; fastest-growing and most complex customer segment. You&#39;ll lead the team responsible for guiding mid-market customers from contract signature through go-live, adoption, and a clean transition to Account Management. You&#39;ll build the frameworks, standards, metrics, and team capability that make that experience world-class and repeatable at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll inherit a team of dedicated ICs and leads that have been experimenting with new ways to support these customers and improve their experience. Your charter is to get leadership in place and be maniacal about customer experience while building the project-management rigor that complex mid-market deployments demand. You&#39;ll be measured on onboarding velocity, deployment quality, customer satisfaction, and the long-term retention impact of a strong start.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Onboarding Team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team is passionate about delivering exceptional customer experiences and helping hoteliers succeed with Cloudbeds from day one. We build together with a test-and-learn mindset that encourages innovation, collaboration, and continuous improvement. Every team member is valued and empowered to share feedback, ideas, and insights so we can learn, grow, and improve both as individuals and as a team. Leaders who thrive here are proactive communicators, collaborative problem-solvers, and true customer advocates who enjoy navigating complexity while building the systems and people that scale it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring to the Team:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and develop the Mid-Market Onboarding team — including Onboarding Project Managers and senior coaches — setting clear expectations, performance standards, growth paths, and a culture of accountability and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end onboarding outcomes for mid-market customers from sales handoff through go-live, adoption, and transition to Account Management — diagnosing and fixing execution gaps in training quality, error detection, and deployment velocity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build standardized onboarding frameworks, SOPs, and configuration standards for complex multi-property and 25–100+ room deployments that balance customization with scalability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and own the metrics that matter: onboarding velocity, deployment quality scores, training completion, CSAT/NPS, and early-lifecycle retention — monitoring portfolio health and intervening early on at-risk projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own capacity and staffing planning for the division — forecasting demand, balancing workload across the team, and partnering with leadership on headcount decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a senior escalation point for complex or at-risk mid-market deployments and partner with Account Management on clean, trust-preserving handoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with Sales, Product, Support, Professional Services, and Account Management — bridging what gets sold and what gets delivered, and contributing to the broader strategy for how Cloudbeds serves mid-market and enterprise-adjacent customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Sets You Up for Success:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years in hospitality or hospitality technology, including hands-on customer onboarding or implementation experience and team leadership (time at a hotel, hotel group, or a PMS or hospitality-tech company; OTA or travel-distribution experience on its own does not count)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of building or significantly improving onboarding and implementation functions and frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven people-leadership experience — hiring, coaching, and developing customer-facing teams in a distributed, global environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project-management foundation: scope, milestones, timelines, and risk mitigation applied to complex multi-stakeholder deployments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of hotel operations and the complexity of serving multi-property, mid-market hospitality customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to move fluidly between strategy and execution — you can design the framework and roll up your sleeves to implement it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven: comfortable with KPIs, dashboards, and using insights to drive decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus Skills to Stand Out:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additional language fluency (Spanish, Portuguese) at a business-professional level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience onboarding or implementing customers at a hospitality SaaS or PMS company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with property management systems, payments, or hospitality fintech&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building onboarding or implementation functions at a scale-up stage company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background working with hotel management companies, small chains, or the consultant ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Authorization: &lt;/strong&gt;Please note that applicants must be currently authorized to work in the location where the position is located without requiring visa sponsorship. At this time, Cloudbeds is unable to provide sponsorship for work visas.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-SD1&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;𝗪𝗼𝗿𝗸 𝗔𝘂𝘁𝗵𝗼𝗿𝗶𝘇𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻: Please note that applicants must be currently authorized to work in the location where the position is located without requiring visa sponsorship. At this time, Cloudbeds is unable to provide sponsorship for work visas.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;𝗪𝗵𝗮𝘁 𝘁𝗼 𝗘𝘅𝗽𝗲𝗰𝘁 - 𝗬𝗼𝘂𝗿 𝗝𝗼𝘂𝗿𝗻𝗲𝘆 𝘄𝗶𝘁𝗵 𝗨𝘀&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Behind Cloudbeds&#39; revolutionary technology is a team redefining what&#39;s possible in hospitality. We&#39;re 650+ team members across 40+ countries, bringing together elite engineers, AI architects, world-class designers, hoteliers, and hospitality veterans to solve challenges others haven&#39;t dared to tackle. Our diverse team speaks 30+ languages, but we all share one language: a passion for innovation and travel. From pioneering breakthroughs in machine learning to revolutionizing how hotels operate, we&#39;re not just watching the future of hospitality unfold – we&#39;re coding it, designing it, writing it, and shipping it. If you&#39;re ready to work alongside some of the brightest minds in tech who are obsessed with using AI to transform a trillion-dollar industry, this is your chance to be part of something extraordinary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learn more online at &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cloudbeds.com/&quot;&gt;cloudbeds.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;𝗖𝗹𝗼𝘂𝗱𝗯𝗲𝗱𝘀 &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cloudbeds.com/press/?press_type=company-news&amp;amp;news_category=awards&quot;&gt;𝗔𝘄𝗮𝗿𝗱𝘀&lt;/a&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Winner – Hotel Management Software | HotelTechAwards (2026)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Overall 10 Best Places to Work | HotelTechAwards (2026)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Overall Top 10 Hotelier&#39;s Choice | HotelTechAwards (2026)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Finalist – Property Management Systems (PMS) &amp;amp; Channel Managers | HotelTechAwards (2026)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Most Loved Workplace® Certified (2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deloitte Technology Fast 500 (2024)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;𝗗𝗶𝘀𝗰𝗼𝘃𝗲𝗿 𝗼𝘂𝗿 𝗕𝗲𝗻𝗲𝗳𝗶𝘁𝘀:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote First, Remote Always&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PTO in accordance with local labor requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully Paid Parental Leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Home office stipend based on country of residency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional development courses in Cloudbeds University&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to professional development, including manager training, upskilling, and knowledge transfer&lt;/li&gt;
